{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>the face of the rock</b> — פני in gematria is כלפי, teaching that all Israel were opposite the face of the rock, face to face, and the few held the many." "<b>המן</b> — Three times in the Masorah: המן הסלע, המן העץ, המן הגורן. Just as there the command was repeated, so too here the command was repeated. And the other — המן הגורן or מן היקב — just as there was famine there, so too here, a dry land without water. And a support for the one who says the tree from which the first man ate was wheat — this is המן העץ, המן הגורן. And for the one who says it was a cluster — as written: or מן היקב."], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {1 "The phrase הפר הציווי is obscure; translated hyper-literally as 'the command was repeated,' following the apparent parallelism with the three-fold occurrence of המן."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:22:38.844445339Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}